# rm519, the star in glass (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm519
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier full
written_for rm_hilde_greyby
written_by codex
title the star in glass
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant job=crafter
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=devout drive=steady
quirk sights_a_star_through_the_bottom_of_every_tumbler
likes pickled_herring stars sharp_knife frosty_mornings
dislikes flies rats
fears a_smiling_rival a_blank_vineyard_letter
hopes a_childs_clear_cup a_star_seen_whole
topics work +0.5 prices +0.3 family +0.3 lore +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=frank refuse=firm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# holds a tumbler up to a single bright star, finding a bubble at once and leaving room for one under the foot if the rim is true.

words
oath! = Cloud my furnace | Crack the cooling shelf
saying! = Let the star go through whole | An even rim has no favourite side
starpoint = one white point | the sharp star
footring = a clear foot ring | the thick glass foot
speck = a pin bubble | a silver speck
reeds = the packing reeds | our dry rushes
shear = the hot shears | the clean shears
wheel = a small grinding wheel | my foot wheel
knife = the clean packing knife | a narrow packing blade
sleeve = the straw sleeve | a padded rush case
purple = a wine-coloured streak | a twist of purple
shard = a flawed scrap | one cloudy shard
seal = a knotted seal | a wax tag
herring = my vinegar fish | the pickled fillet
frostpane = a frost flower | a white star of ice
ledge = the cooling ledge | a brick shelf
lipglass = a thin drinking edge | the finished lip
crossbar = a wooden division | a light crate rail
strawhole = a gap in the packing | a little chink in the reeds

any
opinion @1 church for 1 : The Bright One gave light enough for finding flaws; a plain admission of one is the least I owe.
opinion @2 dole for 1 : Hungry hands shouldn't have to earn the first mouthful by proving how low they have fallen.
opinion @3 drink against 1 : I can make a clean cup without praising everything a wolf chooses to pour into it.
opinion @4 merchants for 1 : A cup costs me rushes and a crate before it costs anybody at market a penny.
opinion @5 road against 1 : A rut gets paid for at my counter in broken feet and chipped rims.
opinion @6 watch for 1 : I can look steadily through a glass while the street patrol gives its attention to the door.
opinion @7 city for 1 : There's enough fire in our city for my work and enough night above it for my own pleasure.
opinion @8 houses mixed 0 : A seal on a crate settles the sender's name. It doesn't settle the quality of the goods.
opinion @9 strangers mixed 0 : A stranger may examine exactly the same tumbler I'd show a cousin.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Come where the pane is clearest.
line @2 greet [here.time=dawn] : A white morning for seeing the fine scratches.
line @3 greet [here.weather=rain] : Room here beyond the darkest wet patch.
line @4 greet [self.working=yes] : Keep back a wrist's width from the ledge. Welcome.
line @5 greet.return : A greeting plainly given and plainly received.
line @6 greet.return [pair.band=friends] : A known face through a clear pane.
line @7 farewell : Carry the fragile end high.
line @8 farewell.return : May good light go with you.
line @9 again.open : The same star comes back into my sight.
line @10 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : A family face belongs beside the good light.
line @11 hail [pair.band=friends] : Look this way through the clear bottom!
line @12 react.news : Say which detail you yourself could hold to the light yourself.
line @13 react.news.new : I haven't seen that glint on the shelf before.
line @14 react.news.known : A second view of a familiar outline.
line @15 react.news.doubt : Too many wavering edges to be sure of the middle.
line @16 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'll set everything fragile aside and stay with you.
line @17 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage] : A bright piece of word. I'll carry that with care.
line @18 answer.how : Steady at the rim and warm in the middle.
line @19 decline : I couldn't put my mark on that promise with a clear mind.
line @20 accept_decline : A straightforward refusal won't crack anything between us.
line @21 sympathise : No call to look straight into the strongest light just now.
line @22 thank : That gives my work a sounder footing.
line @23 deflect_thanks : I'd sooner see the cup arrive whole than be thanked for the packing.
line @24 preclose : The light's shifting off my best testing place.
line @25 accept_preclose : I'll make a clear passage between the crates.
line @26 farewell [here.time=night] : Look up once if the street gives you room.
line @27 answer.how [self.working=yes] : Heat in the wrists and a steady breath so far.
line @28 greet [pair.band=friends] : Leave a little thumb mark where I'll know it's yours.
line @29 greet.return [here.time=night] : There's a face the night hasn't dimmed much.
line @30 preclose [here.time=dusk] : My first testing star will soon be out.
line @31 farewell.return [here.weather=rain] : Wrap the reeds before you cross the square.
scene star
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sight #starpoint# through #footring# once the ware is cool.
b : What if you see two lights?
a : Turn the cup. If one point travels there's #speck# in the foot.

scene frost
when topic=weather self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've tried to copy #frostpane# in a plain drinking glass.
b : Did you manage the fine twigs?
a : Only the thick stem. The frost writes smaller than my shears ever will.

scene knife
when topic=smalltalk self.likes=sharp_knife
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like #knife# to go clean through the rush without bending it.
b : Would a bent rush really cost you a cup?
a : A kink won't spring back after a jolt. I want the spring left in #sleeve#.

scene pickle
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : #herring# looks finer to me in plain glass than on bright tin.
b : For the gleam of the silver skin?
a : For the brine going clear at the edge. Then I can see any stray scale.
b : You've set the dish to work as hard as the fish.

scene fly
when topic=food self.dislikes=flies
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : A fly under a glass cover is more vexing than one outside.
b : At least the cover makes it easy to find.
a : Yes. There I am on one side of good glass watching a fly eat my meal on the other.

scene rats
when topic=work self.dislikes=rats
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Something has chewed one corner of #reeds# down to a brush.
b : Is the ware packed already?
a : Only the lower course. I'll lift it out before a loose glass finds its neighbour.

scene job
when topic=work self.job=crafter self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I draw the last bit of extra glass away with #shear#.
b : Does that leave a nick in the mouth?
a : Unless I turn the lip in the heat. The last slow turn is what the drinker feels.

scene breath
when topic=work
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : Where should I mark a place in a long count of turns?
b : Use a mark you can hear while your eyes stay on the heat.
a : I can tap the iron against the rest lightly. Once a turn without a glance away.

scene duty
when topic=family self.child
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I want to give #self.child# a cup shaped for a small hand.
b : Does it need a handle?
a : A thick low foot first. There's less to pull over and a better chance for a second drink.

scene cousin
when topic=family
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I get a letter out of the vineyards I often see #purple# on the outer fold.
b : Can you read over the stain?
a : I can read what's inside. The outside sometimes brings me a whole hillside's scent.

scene rival
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I weigh rival-house assurances on my own counter.
b : A good seal can protect both sides.
a : Protection starts when I've seen what's under #seal#. I don't claim to see through wax.

scene prayer
when topic=lore
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before gathering glass I give thanks for my sight. The Bright One deserves that pause.
b : Is sight so much of a gift at the furnace?
a : If you catch a thin spot before the glass cools you can spare somebody a nasty break.

scene crate
when topic=travel
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm going to move #crossbar# two fingers inward on my carrying crate.
b : What will that do for the journey?
a : Stop the short cups leaning on the taller row. I'd rather every rim travelled alone.

scene road
when topic=travel world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : A cart overdue leaves me wondering what happened to the packing on the way.
b : Can you check anything before the ropes come off?
a : I can listen for a loose foot against a rail as the load settles.

scene lean
when topic=prices world.times=hard|lean
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : I'd sell a small plain cup during lean trading, keeping the price readable.
b : Couldn't you pass a faulty one off a little cheaper?
a : If the flaw stays in the foot I'll mark it for a buyer to judge. A sharp lip stays with me.

scene offer
when topic=food
does offer / accept / assess
a : There's room for another piece of herring in this glass dish.
b : I'll take a little from the thin end.
a : The brine runs downhill there. Good place for a piece to pick up flavour.

scene starnest
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamed a star had made a nest inside a flawed tumbler.
b : Did you try to let it out?
a : I turned the rim to heaven. There were so many lights I could no longer tell which was mine.

scene support
when topic=work self.hand
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd lay #shard# by the door for #self.hand# to compare with the new batch.
b : Why show a poor piece alongside a sound one?
a : It's an easier lesson when both feet are cooled and nobody has a crate waiting.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd know a cup gone home with #self.friend# by a tiny low swirl.
b : Couldn't another cup have the same mark?
a : Very nearly. I'm thinking of a particular turn I'd be pleased to see used at a familiar table.

scene market
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A buyer ought to feel #lipglass# with a clean finger before any price is agreed.
b : No fear the nicest cup will be marked?
a : A thumb mark washes off. A bad sale stays after every washing.

scene shelf
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I space each warm foot on #ledge# apart from the rest.
b : Are you afraid a row will stick?
a : Afraid one will cool faster on the outside than on the crowded side. Uneven cooling opens cracks.

scene chapel
when topic=lore
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put a simple pane somewhere a chapel seat can catch the early sky.
b : Would it have a colour?
a : No colour from me. The dawn can furnish that part without a bill.

scene lantern
when topic=smalltalk
does give.opinion / disagree / concede
a : A crooked reflection doesn't make the face crooked.
b : It might be comforting to blame every blemish on the pane.
a : Take the pane away. That's a fair test for both the face and the blower.

scene smoke
when topic=land
does tell.feeling / sympathise / assess
a : I have to walk past the roof smoke to get a clean sight of the stars.
b : Do you mind walking so far after the day's heat?
a : The walk's part of cooling. When that testing star comes clear my wrists have stopped aching.

scene seam
when topic=work
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My first glass dish had a foot too grand for its little body.
b : Did it at least stand up well?
a : Like a stump. You needed two hands for a dish that held three spoonfuls.

scene quote
when topic=prices
does ask.advice / give.advice / assess
a : What would you want on a bill for a single glass?
b : A plain total and a warning if the crate has to come back.
a : I'll put the returnable crate on a separate line. A buyer may have a sleeve already.

scene quiet
when topic=smalltalk
does offer / accept / assess
a : Hold this cooled scrap up to the light if you'd like.
b : I can see the edge of the window twice.
a : That's the flaw I've been describing. The glass tells it more plainly than I could.

scene riddle
when topic=pastimes
does tease / tease.return / laugh
a : I see a star in my hand nearly every fine night.
b : I'd call that a poor handful if I couldn't put it in a pocket.
a : Right. The glass fits a pocket but stars prefer their own lodgings.

scene woodbox
when topic=season
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Wet autumn rushes worry me more than frost on the road.
b : Can't you dry a stack in the furnace room?
a : At the distant wall, leaving air between the bundles. I want springy rushes, not tinder.

scene fare
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wonder if the vineyard stars seem closer above the last row.
b : Would a letter carry an answer?
a : A line describing one clear night might get nearer than a choice of distances.

story twinpoint [topic=pastimes]
  : I tested a new tumbler on a point that refused to look properly single.
  : I turned the glass twice. The lights stayed a pair.
  b : Had your eyes grown tired?
  : One was a lamp in an upper window. The star was innocent and so was my tumbler.

story fishscale [topic=food]
  : I kept a fine glass dish back from market because a silver flake clung to its foot.
  : Scrubbing took the flake right off.
  b : A fish scale from dinner?
  : Exactly. I had condemned a good dish for keeping the same company as its maker.

story firstfoot [topic=work]
  : My first attempt at a little drinking glass had a solemn great foot fit for a lamp.
  : I set it sideways to inspect the proportion.
  b : What happened to the big foot?
  : Held the whole thing tipped up like a wheelbarrow. I kept it for my little tools.

story reedwind [topic=travel]
  : A gust once blew through a crate and made a sound like a glass lip struck by iron.
  : I unwrapped the entire top row.
  b : How many cups had broken?
  : None. One hollow reed had learnt to whistle. I cut it shorter for the next journey.

story cousinleaf [topic=family]
  : Vineyard news once reached me with a leaf pressed into the fold.
  : I traced the outline on waste glass and held it to the sun.
  b : Was the leaf green in the copy?
  : Clear. It filled itself with whatever colour I let behind it. Quite a travelled leaf by dusk.

rule @turntest
when concept=bark self.job=crafter self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One more turn on the rest. Let the lip come round.

rule @carton
when concept=bark self.role=merchant self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Each foot apart. Listen while the crate rocks.

rule @starpin
when concept=bark self.likes=stars
does aside
cooldown 8h
say That point moves with the pane. A bubble then.

rule @cutrush
when concept=bark self.likes=sharp_knife
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rush cut square with all its spring left.

rule @coldglass
when concept=bark self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Ice has the finest hand at the window again.

rule @vinegarmeal
when concept=bark self.likes=pickled_herring
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Brine clear round the little silver edge.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : My name is #self.first#. You can look through either end of the tumbler.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you've caught a decent slant of daylight.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : Come far enough from the glare to see the test star.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll keep the ware on the ledge while we speak.
dlg @5 resident.job [self.job=crafter self.workplace] : I work glass at #self.workplace#. Sight down a foot if you'd like to know what my day is worth.
dlg @6 resident.job : I choose work whose flaws I can actually point to.
dlg @7 resident.bye : Keep a soft space between the cups on your way.
dlg @8 shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Light on the counter for inspecting the ware. I'll say which marks are flaws.
dlg @9 shop.greet [here.shop=bare] : Rush sleeves here and nothing left to put inside one.
dlg @10 shop.greet [here.shop=asleep] : The light on this counter is out for now.
dlg @11 shop.prices : The price includes an even rim. I'll quote the packing separately.
dlg @12 shop.bye : Carry a single glass in the middle of its rush sleeve.
dlg @13 resident.hub [here.weather=rain] : There are worse things than rain for looking through clean glass.
dlg @14 resident.job [self.role=merchant] : I count the ware sound only after it's been packed and carried.
graft resident.hub
choice Can a cup really hold a star? -> cuplight
node cuplight
say Hold #footring# between yourself and a single point of light. If the star stays sharp, the cup has passed one of my tests.
choice What if I see a pair? -> doublelight
choice I'll take your word for now. -> hub
node doublelight
say Turn the foot slowly. If the twin travels with your hand, you're holding the cause of its existence.
choice There was something else. -> hub
choice Clear skies to you. -> bye

graft shop.greet
choice How should I pack a pair? [here.shop=open] -> rushpair
node rushpair
say Each foot gets a separate little sleeve. I'll slip #crossbar# between them if you mean to go by cart.
choice How can I check the packing? -> rushmusic
choice Let's see the counter. -> greet
node rushmusic
say Give the crate a gentle shift with both hands under it. The only sound you ought to hear is dry rush moving against the wood.
choice Back to the ware. -> greet
choice Good trading. -> bye
